INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/cnidaria/coralhard/acroporidae/astreopora.md', 'astreopora', 'Pebble coral', 'published', '
## Where seen?
This hard coral with a pebbly surface is sometimes seen on some of our Southern shores.

## Features
Colonies large (about 20cm or more). Colonies are solid (massive) and may be dome-shaped or encrusting, with a few species forming tiers of thick plates. Corallites small, circular opening (1cm or less), usually in a blunt conical shape. The many conical shapes result in a pebbled appearance. The corallites and the surface between corallites usually covered with tiny bumps. New corallites emerge in between existing corallites. The polyps look like tiny sea anemones with 24 tentacles that are flat and petal-like, and a thick body column. Extended polyps usually only seen at night. Colours seen include brown, blue, green sometimes with tinges of other colours.

**Sometimes mistaken**
for
*[Turbinaria](../../dendrophylliidae/Dendrophylliidae)
or
[Echinopora](../../merulinidae/echinopora)*
species.
****
**Status:**
While two species are listed as Near Threatened, there is inadequate information as at 2024 to make an informed assesment of the conservation status of the recorded Pebble corals in Singapore.
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}

---
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery2 %}**Species are difficult to positively identify without close examination.

On this website, they are grouped by external features for convenience of display.*

---

**Pebble corals on Singapore shores**

On
[wildsingapore flickr](http://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/)

- [Photos](https://www.flickr.com/search/?user_id=54527470@N00&sort=date-posted-desc&view_all=1&text=Astreopora)
for free download
- [Map of sightings in Singapore](https://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/tags/Astreopora/map?&fLat=1.2626&fLon=103.8668&zl=11&order_by=recent)

