INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/cnidaria/coralhard/faviidae/hexa/hexasmooth.md', 'hexasmooth', 'Smooth hexagonal corals', 'published', '
## Where seen?
This hard coral is seen on many of our shores

## Features

Colonies 20-30cm, usually irregular dome-shaped. Corallites hexagonal (1cm) with a smooth surface in between the corallites. Often seen with tentacles extended. Colours brown, blue and green, smooth surface usually a pale colour, sometimes with polyp centres in a contrasting colour.

Some species of corals recorded for Singapore that have these patterns include:
*Leptastrea purpurea*
. It''s hard to distinguish them without close examination of small features and they are grouped here by large external features for convenience of display.

**Sometimes confused with**
[Neat hexa corals](../../../siderastreidae/hexaneat)
(*Pseudosiderastrea tayamai*) which belong to Family Siderastreidae.
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}

---
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery2 %}

**Species are difficult to positively identify without close examination.

On this website, they are grouped by external features for convenience of display.*

---

**Smooth hexagonal corals on Singapore shores**

On
[wildsingapore flickr](http://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/)

- [Photos](https://www.flickr.com/search/?user_id=54527470@N00&sort=date-posted-desc&view_all=1&text=Smooth hexagonal coral)
for free download
- [Map of sightings in Singapore](https://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/tags/Smooth%2520hexagonal%2520coral/map?&fLat=1.2629&fLon=103.8654&zl=11&order_by=recent)

---

**Other sightings on Singapore shores**

---
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery3 %}
