INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/cnidaria/coralhard/faviidae/hexa/hexatiny.md', 'hexatiny', 'Tiny hexagonal corals', 'published', '
## Where seen?
Hard corals with very tiny irregular hexagonal corallites are sometimes seen on our Southern shores.

## Features

Colonies seen 10-20cm, sometimes much larger (30-40cm). The colony is generally a smooth boulder shape, but somewhat irregular and not always perfectly spherical. The corallites tiny (less than 1cm) have shared walls and form tiny irregular cells of different shapes and sizes, but generally with about six sides. The result is a rather irregular pattern of hexagons. Colony colours seen include beige, brown and blue.

Some species of corals recorded for Singapore that have these patterns include:
*Goniastrea,*
*Leptastrea*
and
*Platygyra*
**
species.
It''s hard to distinguish them without close examination of small features and they are grouped here by large external features for convenience of display.

{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}
---
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery2 %}**Species are difficult to positively identify without close examination.

On this website, they are grouped by external features for convenience of display.*

---

**Tiny hexagonal corals on Singapore shores**

On
[wildsingapore flickr](http://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/)

- [Photos](https://www.flickr.com/search/?user_id=54527470@N00&sort=date-posted-desc&view_all=1&text=Tiny hexagonal coral)
for free download
- [Map of sightings in Singapore](https://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/tags/Tiny%2520hexagonal%2520coral/map?&fLat=1.2629&fLon=103.8654&zl=11&order_by=recent)

---

**Other sightings on Singapore shores**

---
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery3 %}
