INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/cnidaria/coralhard/merulinidae/mycedium.md', 'mycedium', 'Elephant-nose plate', 'published', '
## Where seen?
This hard coral forms a thick plate with large bumps. It is rarely encountered on the intertidal.

## Features

Colonies 20-30cm. Encrusting plate, thick. Large cup-shaped corallites (about 1.5cm) that look like a nose. Polyp tentacles are only extended at night.
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}

**Species are difficult to positively identify without close examination.

On this website, they are grouped by external features for convenience of display.*

---

**Elephant-nose plate corals on Singapore shores**

On
[wildsingapore flickr](http://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/)

- [Photos](https://www.flickr.com/search/?user_id=54527470%40N00&view_all=1&text=Mycedium%20elephantotus)
for free download
- [Map of sightings in Singapore](https://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/tags/Mycedium%2520elephantotus/map?&fLat=1.2626&fLon=103.8661&zl=11&order_by=recent)

---

**Other sightings on Singapore shores**

---
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery2 %}
---
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery3 %}
---
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery4 %}
---

***Mycedium*
species recorded for Singapore**
Danwei Huang, Karenne P. P. Tun, L. M Chou and Peter A. Todd. 30 Dec 2009.
*An inventory of zooxanthellate sclerectinian corals in Singapore including 33 new records*
**the species found on many shores in Danwei''s paper.

**[Family Merulinidae](../../faviidae/faviidae)**

*Mycedium elephantotus*

---
