INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/cnidaria/coralsoft/nepspiky.md', 'nepspiky', 'Spiky flowery soft coral', 'published', '
## Where seen?
This flowery soft coral with spikes common on some of our shores. On coral rubble near living reefs.

## Features

Colony bushy about 6-12cm. Colony is branched with ''stems'' emerging from a central ''trunk''. The ''stem'' white or transparent, with sclerites embedded in the tissues. The polyps appear in clusters at the tips of the branches. Polyps tiny (about 0.5cm) with eight branched tentacles. The polyps may be white, beige, yellow, orange to purple and maroon. There are spikes next to the polyps, sometimes nearly as large as the polyps. The spikes are more obvious when the polyp tentacles are retracted and the polyps curl up into little balls. The animals do not have symbiotic algae (zooxanthellae) and thus can be found in murky water and dark places.
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}

---
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery2 %}
---
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery3 %}**Flowery friends:**
Tiny animals may be found on spiky flowery soft corals. These include tiny
[false cowrie snails](../../../mollusca/gastropoda/ovulidae/ovulidae)
, tiny
[red-nose shrimps](/wildfacts/guides/crustacea/crustacea/othercrust/shrimp/rednose)
and
[tiny colourful brittle stars](../../../echinodermata/ophiuroidea/tinycolourful)
.

{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery4 %}**ID awaits confirmation. Species are difficult to positively identify without close examination.

On this website, they are grouped by external features for convenience of display*

---

**Spiky flowery soft corals on Singapore shores**

On
[wildsingapore flickr](http://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/)

- [Photos](https://www.flickr.com/search/?user_id=54527470@N00&sort=date-posted-desc&view_all=1&text=Stereonephthya)
for free download
- [Map of sightings in Singapore](https://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/tags/stereonephthya/map?&fLat=1.2629&fLon=103.8661&zl=11&order_by=recent)

---

**Other sightings on Singapore shores**

---
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery5 %}
---

****
