INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/cnidaria/jellyfish/huge.md', 'huge', 'Huge jellyfish', 'published', '
## Where seen?
Enormous jellyfishes are sometimes seen washed ashore on our shores. Several may be seen, and then none seen again for some time. These are probably different species but are grouped here for convenience of display.

## Features

Bell about 25-50cm diameter, oral arms about the same length as bell diameter (they seldom extend much beyond the bell). Some have finger-like bumps on the bell.

**Jelly friends:**
Small fish have been seen sheltering among their arms.
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}

---
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery2 %}**Species are difficult to positively identify without close examination.

On this website, the animals are grouped by external features for convenience of display.*

---

**Huge jellyfishes on Singapore shores**

On
[wildsingapore flickr](http://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/)

- [Photos](https://www.flickr.com/search/?user_id=54527470%40N00&sort=date-posted-desc&view_all=1&text=Huge%20jellyfish)
for free download
- [Map of sightings in Singapore](https://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/tags/huge%20jellyfish/map?&fLat=1.2626&fLon=103.8661&zl=11&order_by=recent)

---

**Other sightings on Singapore shores**

---
