INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/crustacea/crab/menippidae/rumphii.md', 'rumphii', 'Maroon stone ', 'published', '
## Where seen?
This sturdy crab is seen in rocky and rubbly areas on our Northern shores. Elsewhere, it is found in sandy-muddy areas usually under rocks.

## Features

Body width to about 9cm. Large oval body, edge smooth with four blunt points or ''teeth''. Between the eyes are four tiny bumps arranged in a square. Reddish to pinkish brown and maroon in adults; young crabs maroon to reddish brown, with longitudinal white stripes. Large pincers smooth (no pimples) with black tips. One pincer slightly larger with a large molar-like tooth at the base of the finger. Walking legs not very hairy. Its eyes are all red without any green, unlike
the very similar looking
[Stone crab](hardwickii)
(*Myomenippe hardwickii*).

**Sometimes mistaken for**
the
[Stone crab](hardwickii)
(*Myomenippe hardwickii*) and
[Red egg crab](../../xanthidae/integerrimus)
(*Atergatis integerrimus*).
Here''s more on how to tell apart
[big crabs with big pincers](../../../bigpincer)
seen on our rocky shores and coral rubble.
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}

---

**Maroon stone crabs on Singapore shores**

On
[wildsingapore flickr](http://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/)

- [Photos](https://www.flickr.com/search/?user_id=54527470%40N00&sort=date-posted-desc&view_all=1&text=Menippe%20rumphii)
for free download
- [Map of sightings in Singapore](https://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/tags/Menippe%2520rumphii/map?&fLat=1.2629&fLon=103.8661&zl=11&order_by=recent)

