INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/crustacea/crab/xanthidae/actaea.md', 'actaea', 'Ruby reef crab ', 'published', '
## Where seen?
This tiny jewel of a crab was seen once on Labrador.

## Features

Body width 1-2cm. Body and claws bright red with bumps and ridges. Like other brightly coloured Xanthid crabs, it is probably
[poisonous](xanthidae)
.
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery2 %}

---

**Ruby reef crabs on Singapore shores**

On
[wildsingapore flickr](http://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/)

- [Photos](https://www.flickr.com/search/?user_id=54527470@N00&sort=date-posted-desc&view_all=1&text=Ruby reef crab)
for free download
- [Map of sightings in Singapore](https://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/tags/Ruby%2520reef%2520crab/map?&fLat=1.2622&fLon=103.8661&zl=11&order_by=recent)

---

**Acknowledgements**
With grateful thanks to Prof Leo Tan for finding this crab. And to Ondrej Radosta for correcting the identity of the crab.
