---
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery5 %}
---
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery6 %}
---

**Acknowledgements**

Grateful thanks to Dominik Kneer for correcting the identification of these animals. Those with orange claws are not
*Glypturus*
as originally stated, but a species of
*Corallianassa*
. One of the animals is identified as
*Axiopsis serratifrons*
in another Family Axiidea. Family Callianassidae and Family Axiidae belong in infraorder Axiidae.
