INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/echinodermata/holothuroidea/tinyred.md', 'tinyred', 'Tiny red sea cucumber', 'published', '
## Where seen?
This tiny sea cucumbers are sometimes seen on our Northern shores. In groups of many individuals, densely carpeting a few square metres. They settle on seaweeds and coral rubble areas, clinging to sponges, seaweeds, even other larger sea cucumbers and encrusting organisms covering the coral rubble.

## Features

About 1cm or shorter. Often mistaken for worms, each has all the features that bigger sea cucumbers have. Body bright red, squarish or quadrangular in cross-section, backside tip translucent white. Tiny tube feet, very long, white. Feeding tentacles dark at the base becoming yellowish at tips, branched tips translucent white.
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery2 %}

**Species are difficult to positively identify without close examination.*
*On this website, they are grouped by external features for convenience of display*

---

**Tiny red sea cucumbers on Singapore shores**

On
[wildsingapore flickr](http://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/)

- [Photos](https://www.flickr.com/search/?user_id=54527470%40N00&sort=date-posted-desc&view_all=1&text=tiny%20red%20sea%20cucumber)
for free download
- [Map of sightings in Singapore](https://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/tags/%2522Tiny%2520red%2520sea%2520cucumber%2522/map?&fLat=1.2626&fLon=103.8661&zl=11&order_by=recent)

---

**Other sightings on Singapore shores**

---
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery3 %}
---

### References

- Lane, David J.W. and Didier Vandenspiegel. 2003
*. A Guide to Sea Stars and Other Echinoderms of Singapore*
. Singapore Science Centre. 187pp.
