INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/mollusca/bivalvia/pectinidae/large.md', 'large', 'Large scallop', 'published', '
## Where seen?
These large clams are sometimes seen on our Southern shores near living reefs.

## Features

Diameter 6-10cm. A circular two-part shell, thick and heavy, yellowish, often covered in sediments. When submerged, a fringe of tentacles emerge, some long and many short tentacles, with many tiny, well developed eyes along the mantle edge.

**Clap back clam**
**:**
It can ''swim'' backwards with claps of its shell.
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}

**Species are difficult to positively identify without close examination.

On this website, they are grouped by external features for convenience of display.*

---

