INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/mollusca/bivalvia/veneridae/dispar.md', 'dispar', 'Discrepant venus clam', 'published', '
## Where seen?
This clam is sometimes seen on sandy shores.
Elsewhere, they are found on intertidal shores with sand.

## Features

About 4-6cm. Shell thick with fine ribs and usually a pattern of fine broken lines.

*![](https://images.naturehungry.sg/mollusca/bivalvia/veneridae/dispar/050510tusg6133m3.jpg)

Tuas, May 05*

**Species are difficult to positively identify without close examination.

On this website, they are grouped by external features for convenience of display.*

---

**Acknowledgements**

With grateful thanks to André Sartori from
[eBivalvia](http://ebivalvia.lifedesks.org/)
on EOL''s Life Desk for identifying this clam.
