INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/mollusca/gastropoda/architectonicidae/perdix.md', 'perdix', 'Patridge sundial snail', 'published', '
## Where seen?
Sometimes seen on sandy areas near seagrasses on some of our shores.

## Features

6-8cm in diameter. Shell thick and coils to fom a disc with a flat base. Shell pattern of spirals of brown bars on a paler background. Body and fat tentacles are plain (not striped). Operculum thin, flat and made of a horn-like material.

**What does it eat?**
It is said to eat burrowing sea anemones and sea pens. The mouth region is lined with a tough cuticle as a protection against stings of their prey.
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}

---

