INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/mollusca/gastropoda/architectonicidae/variegatus.md', 'variegatus', 'Variegated sundial snail', 'published', '
## Where seen?
The snail with a unique operculum is sometimes seen on our Southern shores.

## Features

Up to 2cm in diameter. Shell thick and coiled to form an overall conical shape. Coils have a beaded texture, colours usually alternating dark and light. The operculum is conical with regular grooves and resembles a drill! Body mottled with long tentacles.

**What does it eat?**
It feeds on
[zoanthids](../../../../cnidaria/others/zoanthid/zoanthid)
and is said to be always found in close association with zoanthids.

**Baby sundials:**
It lays long egg strings.
