INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/mollusca/gastropoda/cypraeidae/walkeri.md', 'walkeri', 'Walker''s cowrie', 'published', '
## Where seen?
This small cowrie has so far only been seen at Cyrene Reef. It is globally considered uncommon. It was previously known as
*Cypraea walkeri*
or
*Erronea walkeri walkeri*
.

## Features

2-2.5cm. Shell somewhat pear-shaped, generally pale blue with 3 dark brown bands, centre band much broader, outer bands may be broken up into squares. Underside pale violet with brown spots and short, dark violet ''teeth''. The living animal has a red mantle
with white branching finger-like structures (papillae) while the foot is red with some white dots or blotches.
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}

---

**Walker''s cowries on Singapore shores**

On
[wildsingapore flickr](http://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/)

- [Photos](https://www.flickr.com/search/?user_id=54527470@N00&sort=date-posted-desc&view_all=1&text=Contradusta walkeri)
for free download
- [Map of sightings in Singapore](https://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/tags/Contradusta%2520walkeri/map?&fLat=1.2619&fLon=103.8674&zl=11&order_by=recent)

---

**Other sightings on Singapore shores**

---
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery2 %}
---
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery3 %}
---

**Acknowledgements**
Grateful thanks to Chim Chee Kong for identifying this snail on
[his flickr](http://www.flickr.com/photos/chimck/2698539046/)
