INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/mollusca/gastropoda/ellobiidae/banded.md', 'banded', 'Banded mangrove ear snail', 'published', '
## Where seen?
This snail is sometimes seen in our back mangroves, on and around the base of mangrove trees. It breathes air (instead of through gills like most other marine snails). It was previously known as
*Cassidula mustelina.*
The shell opening resembles an ear.

## Features

2-3cm. Shell thick and oval, with wide dark and light brown spiralling bands. Underside pinkish violet around the shell opening. Species of mangrove ear snails are not easy to tell apart in the field

**What does it eat?**
It grazes on algae growing on mangrove trees and on the ground.
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}

---

**Banded mangrove ear snails on Singapore shores**

On
[wildsingapore flickr](http://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/)

- [Photos](https://www.flickr.com/search/?user_id=54527470%40N00&sort=date-posted-desc&view_all=1&text=Cassidula%20nucleus)
for free download
- [Map of sightings in Singapore](https://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/tags/Cassidula%20nucleus/map?&fLat=1.3148&fLon=103.8434&zl=11&order_by=recent)

---

**Other sightings on Singapore shores**

---
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery2 %}
---
