INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/mollusca/gastropoda/littorinidae/rock.md', 'rock', 'Rock periwinkle snail', 'published', '
## Where seen?
This small snail is often seen on many of our rocky shores. At low tide, it is usually seen in groups wedged into crevices and cracks in rocks. At night and on cool, rainy days, they actively move about in large numbers on the rocks or among seaweeds growing on the rocks.
****
## Features

0.8-1cm. Shells thin and smooth with fine grooves. Colours variable from black to light with brown speckles or stripes.
Operculum thin, circular, brown and made from a horn-like material. The animal has short tentacles.

Species are difficult to positively identify without close examination. On this website, the various kinds of tiny periwinkle snails found on rocks are grouped here for convenience of display.
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}
**Species are difficult to positively identify without close examination.

On this website, they are grouped by external features for convenience of display.*

---

**Rock periwinkle snails on Singapore shores**

On
[wildsingapore flickr](http://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/)

- [Photos](https://www.flickr.com/search/?user_id=54527470@N00&sort=date-posted-desc&view_all=1&text=Rock periwinkle snail)
for free download
- [Map of sightings in Singapore](https://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/tags/Rock%2520periwinkle%2520snail/map?&fLat=1.2626&fLon=103.8661&zl=11&order_by=recent)

---

**Other sightings on Singapore shores**

---
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery2 %}
---
