INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/mollusca/gastropoda/naticidae/spotted.md', 'spotted', 'Spotted moon snail ', 'published', '
## Where seen?
This moon snail with a spotted body is sometimes seen on sandy areas near reefs on some of our Southern shores
.
It is also known as Gualtieri''s moon snail.

## Features

2-3cm. Shell smooth thick spherical (not flat) with the spiral tip sticking out. Shell pattern beige, grey or orange sometimes with broad darker bands overlaid with many thin dark bands. On the underside, a small comma-shaped depression. Operculum pearly white with a dark smudge where the whorl starts, smooth (no grooves). Body white with dark spots all over, tentacles short.

{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery2 %}
## Human uses

It is collected for food and the shell trade.

{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery3 %}
---

**Spotted moon snails on Singapore shores**

On
[wildsingapore flickr](http://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/)

- [Photos](https://www.flickr.com/search/?user_id=54527470@N00&sort=date-posted-desc&view_all=1&text=Natica gualteriana)
for free download
- [Map of sightings in Singapore](https://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/tags/Natica%2520gualteriana%2520/map?&fLat=1.2619&fLon=103.8661&zl=11&order_by=recent)

