INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/mollusca/gastropoda/pyramidellidae/auriscati.md', 'auriscati', 'Cat''s ear pyramid snail', 'published', '
## Where seen?
This snail is sometimes seen in sandy sheltered man-made lagoons on our Southern shores. Often, a pair or a handful are seen among the more numerous
[Bazillion snails](../../potamididae/zonalis)
. According to Abbott, it is uncommon. It is among the larger of the
[pyramid snails](pyramidellidae)
, which are mostly very tiny parasitic snails.

## Features

2-2.5cm. Shell thick conical with a pointed tip. Shell opening large ear-shaped white. Shell texture ribbed spirals, colour white with spirals of brown smudged spots, sometimes plain orange. Operculum oval, thin, made of a horn-like material, yellowish. Body white, with large thin foot and a triangular shaped head with short slender tentacles.
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}

---

**Car''s ear pyramid snails on Singapore shores**

On
[wildsingapore flickr](http://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/)

- [Photos](https://www.flickr.com/search/?user_id=54527470%40N00&sort=date-taken-desc&view_all=1&text=Otopleura%20auriscati)
for free download
- [Map of sightings in Singapore](https://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/tags/Otopleura%20auriscati/map?&fLat=1.2605&fLon=103.8733&zl=11&order_by=recent)

