INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/plants/mangrove/lumnitzera/lumnitzera.md', 'lumnitzera', 'Teruntum ', 'published', '
## Where seen?
This pretty plant with plasticky leaves and tiny flowers is sometimes seen in back mangroves.

## Features

Short shrub to tall tree. Leaves spatula shaped with oval ends thick and fleshy, arranged in a spiral. Flowers small. The small fruits are ribbed, corky and float, and dispersed by water.

**Sometimes mistaken for**
[Chengam](../../scyphiphora/hydrophyllacea)
(*Scyphiphora hydrophyllacea*) which has its leaves arranged in a spiral.

According to Giesen, although occurring throughout Malaysia and Indonesia,
*L. littorea*
and
*L. racemosa*
practically exclude each other in habitat and have never been collected in exactly the same stand. The exact cause of this different ecological behaviour is not yet known.

![](https://images.naturehungry.sg/plants/mangrove/lumnitzera/littorea/090124ubnd6072m3.jpg)

*Pulau Ubin, Jan 09*
![](https://images.naturehungry.sg/plants/mangrove/lumnitzera/racemosa/091115ubnd4196m3.jpg)

*Pulau Ubin,Nov 09*

---

**Teruntum on Singapore shores**

---
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}
---
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery2 %}
---
