INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/plants/seaweed/chlorophyta/daisy.md', 'daisy', 'Daisy green seaweed', 'published', '
## Where seen?
This tiny seaweed is often overlooked. It grows on stones and coral rubble, often near the
[''Taugeh'' seaweed](neomeris)
(*Neomeris*
sp.)

## Features

Tiny cap that is shaped like a daisy (about 0.5cm in diameter) made up of 34 petal-shaped ''rays'', held up on a thin stalk. This tiny seaweed is calcified, in different degrees depending on the species. The young cap is green and turns white as it ages.

![](https://images.naturehungry.sg/plants/seaweed/chlorophyta/daisy/101223sntd3940m3.jpg)

*Sentosa, Dec 10*

{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}**Species are difficult to positively identify without close examination of internal parts.

On this website, they are grouped by external features for convenience of display.*

---

**Daisy green seaweed on Singapore shores**

---

Photos of
[Daisy green seaweed](https://www.flickr.com/search/?q=Parvocaulis+parvulus&w=54527470%40N00&s=rec)
for free download from
[wildsingapore flickr](http://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/)

