INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/plants/seaweed/chlorophyta/valonia.md', 'valonia', 'Beaded cushion green seaweed', 'published', '
## Where seen?
This cushion of little green beads is sometimes seen on our Southern shores growing on hard surfaces near reefs.

## Features

The entire cushion about 2-5cm wide made up of tiny, tightly packed beads. Each translucent bead is a sphere or tear-drop shaped. The beads are actually interconnected. The entire cushion encrusts hard surfaces. Dark to light green or olive green.

**Sometimes mistaken for**
[Bubble green seaweed](boergesenia)
(*Boergesenia forbesii*) which has much larger and more loosely arranged translucent bubble-like shapes. Here''s more on
[how to tell apart some green seaweeds](cfgrapes)
.

According to
[AlgaeBase](http://www.algaebase.org/search/genus/detail/?genus_id=33606)
, there are more than 10 current
*Valonia*
species.

## Human uses

Some species are eaten by people.

![](https://images.naturehungry.sg/plants/seaweed/chlorophyta/valonia/070615sntrg0285m3.jpg)

*Sentosa, Jun 07

![](https://images.naturehungry.sg/plants/seaweed/chlorophyta/valonia/070615sntrg0285m3b.jpg)*

{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}

**Species are difficult to positively identify without close examination of internal parts.

On this website, they are grouped by external features for convenience of display.*

---

**Beaded cushion green seaweeds on Singapore shores**

---

Photos of
[Beaded cushion green seaweeds](https://www.flickr.com/search/?q=Valonia&w=54527470%40N00&s=rec)
for free download from
[wildsingapore flickr](http://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/)

---

Distribution in Singapore on
[this wildsingapore flickr map](https://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/tags/Valonia/map?&fLat=1.2612&fLon=103.865&zl=11&order_by=recent)

---

***Valonia*
species recorded for Singapore**
**
Pham, M. N., H. T. W. Tan, S. Mitrovic & H. H. T. Yeo, 2011.
*A Checklist of the Algae of Singapore*
.

*Valonia aegagropila

Valonia fastigiata

Valonia ventricosa*

