INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/plants/seaweed/phaeophyta/dictyota.md', 'dictyota', 'Y-branch brown seaweed', 'published', '
## Where seen?
This flat strap-like brown seaweed is sometimes seen on many of our shores, often anchored in bare sand.

## Features

A bunch of several to many strap-like blades about 1-2cm wide and 10-15cm long, branching on one plane forming Y-shapes with rounded or squarish tips. The seaweed does not have a prominent midrib or vein. Usually a plain translucent brown. In some, the entire clump comprises a few long strands. In others, there are many short strands forming a dense clump.

According to
[AlgaeBase](http://www.algaebase.org/search/genus/detail/?genus_id=51)
, there are more than 70 current
*Dictyota*
species.

## Human uses

Strap brown seaweed is eaten by people and used as animal feed, medicine for its antibacterial properties.
[*Dictyota dichotoma*](ybranch)
is also used to make beer, frozen food, fruit juices, ice cream, jellies, in meat and flavour sauces, milk shakes, pastries and salad dressings. Extracts from it are also used in industry as emulsifiers, gelling agents, stabilisers.
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}

---
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery2 %}

**Seaweed species are difficult to positively identify without microscopic examination.

On this website, they are grouped by external features for convenience of display.*

---

**Y-branch brown seaweed on Singapore shores**

---

On
[wildsingapore flickr](http://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/)

- [Photos](https://www.flickr.com/search/?text=Dictyota%20sp.&sort=date-taken-desc&user_id=54527470%40N00)
for free download
- [Map of sightings in Singapore](https://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/tags/Dictyota%2520sp./map?&fLat=1.2605&fLon=103.8647&zl=11&order_by=recent)

---

**Other sightings on Singapore shores**

---
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery3 %}
---

***Dictyota*
species recorded for Singapore**
**
Pham, M. N., H. T. W. Tan, S. Mitrovic & H. H. T. Yeo, 2011.
*A Checklist of the Algae of Singapore*
.

*Dictyota adnata

Dictyota bartayresiana

Dictyota ciliolata

Dictyota crispata

[Dictyota dichotoma](ybranch)*
(Bluish y-branch brown seaweed)
*Dictyota dichotoma var. intricata

Dictyota hauckiana

Dictyota lata*

---
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery4 %}
