INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/plants/seaweed/phaeophyta/perforated.md', 'perforated', 'Perforated brown seaweed', 'published', '
## Where seen?
This ''holey'' brown seaweed is sometimes seen often anchored in bare sand in calm shallow areas near reefs on our Southern shores.

## Features

Each clump about 6-10cm. The seaweed is made up of fleshy but narrow strips perforated regularly with many holes of various sizes, forming contorted mesh- or net-like clumps. When young, the seaweed is an irregular sphere. Usually a light or golden brown. ''
*Clathratus*
'' means ''latticed''.

## Human uses

It is eaten by people as a salad mixed with vegetables or as a spice. It is also used as animal feed, fertiliser and medicine.

![](https://images.naturehungry.sg/plants/seaweed/phaeophyta/perforated/1003021hntd9614m3.jpg)
*Pulau Hantu, Mar 10*

{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}

**Seaweed species are difficult to positively identify without microscopic examination.

On this website, they are grouped by external features for convenience of display.*

---

**Perforated brown seaweeds on Singapore shores**

---

