INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/plants/seaweed/rhodophyta/scaly.md', 'scaly', 'Scaly red seaweed ', 'published', '
## Where seen?
On the intertidal, this flat hard circular seaweed encrusts hard surfaces near reefs, often overlapping like fish scales.

## Features

Clusters of flat circular encrusting (2-4cm) disks that have a slippery surface. The disks are hard because they incorporate calcium carbonate on the underside. Most of the disk is stuck to a hard surface, sometimes the edges are free. Often crowded or overlapping. Colour orangey, yellowish brown, chocolate brown to brown.

**Sometimes confused with**
[Bracket brown seaweed](../../phaeophyta/bracket)
(*Lobophora variegata*) which is not so encrusting and is leathery.

According to
[AlgaeBase](http://www.algaebase.org/search/genus/detail/?genus_id=33926)
: there are 72 species of
*Peyssonnelia*
many of them requiring microscopic examination to determine to species.

*![](https://images.naturehungry.sg/plants/seaweed/rhodophyta/scaly/091206tmd5727m3.jpg)

Tanah Merah, Dec 09*

{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}**Seaweed species are difficult to positively identify without microscopic examination.

On this website, they are grouped by external features for convenience of display.*

---

**Scaly red seaweeds on Singapore shores**

---

Photos of
[Scaly red seaweeds](https://www.flickr.com/search/?q=Peyssonnelia&w=54527470%40N00&s=rec)
for free download from
[wildsingapore flickr](http://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/)

---

Distribution in Singapore on
[this wildsingapore flickr map](https://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/tags/Peyssonnelia/map?&fLat=1.2629&fLon=103.864&zl=11&order_by=recent)

---
