INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/porifera/branchpurple.md', 'branchpurple', 'Purple branching sponge', 'published', '
******
## Where seen?
Like a little purple bush, this sponge is commonly seen on hard surfaces near the mid-water mark on our Northern shores.
## Features

A bunch of ''stems'' slender (1-1.5cm thick) and long (10-15cm), usually growing upright but sometimes sprawling horizontally hugging the surface. The stems are not extensively branched and cylindrical with rounded tips (not tapering). With small shallow holes regularly spaced along the length of the ''stem'' (not just at the tips, and the ''stem'' is not a hollow tube). The surface texture is rough. Colours usually purple to lilac.

These sponges are draped with
[sponge synaptid sea cucumbers](../../echinodermata/holothuroidea/synsponge)
at some times of the year.

![](https://images.naturehungry.sg/porifera/branchpurple/060129skdd6619m3.jpg)

*Pulau Sekudu, Jan 06*

{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}
---

{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery2 %}

**Species are difficult to positively identify without close examination.

On this website, they are grouped by external features for convenience of display.*

---

**Purple branching sponges on Singapore shores**

---

Photos of
[Purple branching sponges](https://www.flickr.com/search/?q=Purple+branching+sponge+Callyspongia+sp.&w=54527470%40N00&s=rec)
for free download from
[wildsingapore flickr](http://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/)

---

Distribution in Singapore on
[this wildsingapore flickr map](https://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/tags/Purple%2520branching%2520sponge%2520Callyspongia%2520sp./map?&fLat=1.2626&fLon=103.8661&zl=11&order_by=recent)

---

**Other sightings on Singapore shores**

---
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery3 %}
---
