INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/porifera/rotijala.md', 'rotijala', '''Roti jala'' sponge', 'published', '
## Where seen?
This bright orange jumble of tangled string-like sponge does indeed resemble a local favourite
[Roti Jala](http://hungerhunger.blogspot.sg/2008/03/roti-jala-net-pancakes.html)
. It is sometimes seen on Beting Bronok.

## Features

Bright orange long skinny strings about 0.2cm in diameter, in a tangled jumble that may be 20cm wide. On rubbly areas or tangled on other encrusting organisms. Although the surface may appear smooth, it is rather rough. The strings are fragile.
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}

**Sponge species are difficult to positively identify without close examination.

On this website, they are grouped by external features for convenience of display.*

---

**''Roti jala'' sponges on Singapore shores**

On
[wildsingapore flickr](http://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/)

- [Photos](https://www.flickr.com/search/?q=Terpios&w=54527470@N00&s=rec)
for free download
- [Map of sightings in Singapore](https://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/tags/Terpios/map?&fLat=1.2622&fLon=103.8661&zl=11&order_by=recent)

---

**Other sightings on Singapore shores**

---

### References


- Lim Swee Cheng, Nicole de Voogd and Tan Koh Siang. 2008.
*A Guide to Sponges of Singapore*
. Singapore Science Centre. 173pp.
