INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/vertebrates/fish/haemulidae/pictum.md', 'pictum', 'Painted sweetlips', 'published', '
## Where seen?
The stripy yellow and black juveniles are sometimes seen on some of our shores. Juveniles are seen in weedy areas. Adults are seen on sandy and silty bottoms near reefs.

## Features

Juveniles about 10cm. Slender long body yellow with black stripe through the eye across the body and the tail. And a black stripe above including the dorsal fin. Adults to 90cm, uniformly silvery grey.
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}
**Wiggly swimmer:**
Like some other young sweetlips species, the juvenile Painted sweetlips typically swims by ''wagging'' its large tails resulting in a twisting motion.
**What does it eat?**
It eats small bottom-dwelling animals and fishes.

---

**Painted sweetlips on Singapore shores**

On
[wildsingapore flickr](http://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/)

- [Photos](https://www.flickr.com/search/?user_id=54527470%40N00&sort=date-posted-desc&safe_search=3&view_all=1&text=Diagramma%20pictum)
for free download
- [Map of sightings in Singapore](https://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/tags/Diagramma%2520pictum/map?&fLat=1.2612&fLon=103.8654&zl=11&order_by=recent)

---

**Other sightings on Singapore shores**

