INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/vertebrates/fish/ostraciidae/cubicus.md', 'cubicus', 'Yellow boxfish ', 'published', '
## Where seen?
This cute little cube-like fish was seen once on Pulau Sekudu.

****
## Features

To 45cm, the one seen was about 4cm long and probably a juvenile. It is cube-shaped, bright yellow with many small black dots. As the fish grows older, it will have larger dots or black-edged white eye-like spots. Adults grow to 45cm and are found in deeper waters. They are dusky yellow with irregular yellow lines on the head, with greyish blue fins. It is reported that juveniles are often seen among
*Acropora*
corals.
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}
**What do does it eat?**
It eats mainly seaweeds and also nibbles on tiny animals, sponges, sand dwelling worms, little crustaceans, snails and fishes.

---

**Yellow cowfishes on Singapore shores**

On
[wildsingapore flickr](http://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/)

- [Photos](https://www.flickr.com/search/?text=Ostracion%20cubicus&safe_search=3&sort=date-taken-desc&user_id=54527470%40N00)
for free download
