INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/vertebrates/fish/pomacentridae/prosopotaenia.md', 'prosopotaenia', 'Honey-head damsel ', 'published', '
## Where seen?
Juveniles of this fish are sometimes seen on near our reefs. Elsewhere, adults are found iin lagoons and coastal reefs, usually in silty areas, may be solitary or in groups.

## Features

To 16cm, juveniles seen about 2cm long. Juveniles with a white body, two broad honey brown bars, one through the eyes, and another in the middle of the body, with a large gold-margined black spot on the dorsal fin. The adult looks different, honey brown with a white breast lacking dark blotches, a broad pale bar in the middle of the body, head with blue lines.
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery2 %}

---

**Honey-head damsels on Singapore shores**

On
[wildsingapore flickr](http://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/)

- [Photos](https://www.flickr.com/search/?user_id=54527470%40N00&sort=date-taken-desc&safe_search=3&view_all=1&text=Dischistodus%20prosopotaenia)
for free download
- [Map of sightings in Singapore](https://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/tags/Dischistodus%2520prosopotaenia/map?&fLat=1.2561&fLon=103.8633&zl=11&order_by=recent)

---

**Other sightings on Singapore shores**

---
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery3 %}
---

**Acknowlegement**

Thanks to Jeffrey Low for identifying the adult caught in a fishing net.
