INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('entries', '_entries/worm/polychaeta/sabtinysand.md', 'sabtinysand', 'Tiny sand fanworm', 'published', '
## Where seen?
This tiny fanworm is sometimes seen on some of our shores, usually in silty sandy sheltered lagoons, often in small groups of 2-3 individuals near burrows.

## Features

On this page are included small fanworms with spots found in sandy areas.
Fan about 1cm in diameter.
The small fan is a single spiral, white with brown portions that result in a chevron banded pattern. Some are brownish with white spots. They are highly
sensitive to disturbances and will disappear at the slightest sign of danger.
{% include img-wrap-group.html items=page.galleries.gallery1 %}

***
*Species are difficult to positively identify without close examination.

On this website, they are grouped by external features for convenience of display.*

---

**Tiny sand fanworms on Singapore shores**

On
[wildsingapore flickr](http://www.flickr.com/photos/wildsingapore/)

- [Photos](https://www.flickr.com/search/?user_id=54527470%40N00&sort=date-posted-desc&view_all=1&text=Tiny%20sand%20fanworm)
