**Fishes
with flat heads****How
to tell them apart?***updated Apr 2020*

---

 Several different
kinds of fishes have flat heads. Here''s more on
how to tell them apart.

---

***![](platycephalidae/indicus/030927cjd0083m3.jpg)*  
[Flathead](platycephalidae/platycephalidae.htm)**Family Platycephalidae

***![](gobiidae/biocellatus/100612chgd5276m3.jpg)*[Crocodile flathead goby](gobiidae/biocellatus.htm)**Family Gobiidae

**![](callionymidae/erythraeus/090709chgd6828m3.jpg)[Dragonet](callionymidae/callionymidae.htm)**Family Callionymidae
![](platycephalidae/indicus/030927cjd0083m3c.jpg)
![](gobiidae/biocellatus/100612chgd5276m3a.jpg)
![](callionymidae/erythraeus/090709chgd6828m3a.jpg)
Mouth
huge from ''ear to ear''.  
Long rounded snout.
  
Eyes covered with ''fringe'' or ''eyelids''
Mouth
huge from ''ear to ear''.  
Medium rounded snout.
  
Eyes with a small ''eyelid''.
Mouth
small.  
Short pointed snout.
  

---

**More
comparisons**

---

![](cynoglossidae/cynoglossidae/050622cftd4074m3.jpg)

![](soleidae/ovata/050511cftg6220m3.jpg)

![](paralichthyidae/paralichthyidae/050917smkg2477m3.jpg)

**[Tongue-soles](cynoglossidae/cynoglossidae.htm)**  
Family Cynoglossidae

**[Soles](soleidae/soleidae.htm)**  
Family Soleidae

**[Large-tooth
flounders](paralichthyidae/paralichthyidae.htm)**   
Family Paralichthyidae

---

how to tell apart [flatfish
families commonly seen](pleuronectiformes/pleuronectiformes1.htm)

