INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('articles', '_articles/guides/cflargecnidarians.md', 'cflargecnidarians', 'Large ''hairy'' cnidarians on Singapore shores: how to tell them apart', 'published', 'cnidarians [text
index](cnidariaindex.htm) | [photo index](cnidariafi2.htm)
Phylum [Cnidaria](cnidaria.htm)
**Large
''hairy'' cnidarians  
How to tell them apart?***updated Apr 2020*

---

Several large
cnidarians (50cm and above) covered with ''hairy'' or ''furry'' stuff are
sometimes confused for one another. Here''s more on how to tell them
apart.

---

![](actiniaria/gigantea/070520smkg9484m3.jpg)

![](coralsoft/letpinwheel/070704jngg1241m3.jpg)

![](coralhard/poritidae/gonbig/051204sisd6415m3.jpg)

**[Sea
anemone](actiniaria/actiniaria.htm)**Order
Actiniaria

**[Leathery
soft coral](coralsoft/alcyoniidae.htm)**Order
Alcyonacea

**[Anemone
hard coral](coralhard/poritidae/gonbig.htm)** Order Sclerectina

A
sea anemone is usually  
a single animal.

A
leathery coral is usually   
a colony of many tiny animals.

A
hard coral is usually   
a colony of many tiny animals.

![](actiniaria/gigantea/070520smkg9484m3a.jpg)

![](coralsoft/letpinwheel/070704jngg1242m3a.jpg)

![](coralhard/poritidae/gonbig/051204sisg3282m3a.jpg)

The
sea anemone has   
a central mouth.
The
leathery coral colony does not have a central mouth. The leathery
tissue is shared by the tiny polyps.
The
hard coral colony does not have a central mouth. The hard skeleton
is created by the tiny polyps.
The
''hairy'' things on the disk   
are tentacles.
The
''hairy'' things are actually   
tiny polyps, each with a tiny   
central mouth and tentacles.
The
''hairy'' things are actually   
tiny polyps, each with a tiny   
central mouth and tentacles.

---

**More
comparisons**
  

---

![](others/corallimorphs/carpet/040410sisbd0053m3.jpg)  
Many individual
[corallimorphs](others/corallimorphs/corallimorph.htm)
crowded
together may seem to be a large carpet.

![](actiniaria/beadbanded/060114cjg3882m3.jpg)  
Many individual
[banded bead anemones](actiniaria/beadbanded.htm)  crowded together may seem to be
a large carpet.

![](others/zoanthid/various/070518tkrg9359m3b.jpg)  
Many individual
[zoanthids](others/zoanthid/zoanthid.htm)  crowded together
may seem to be a large carpet.

---

These are some large
[sea anemones](actiniaria/actiniaria.htm) with a close up look
at their tentacles.  

![](actiniaria/haddoni/050724bbd5311m3.jpg)

*![](actiniaria/doreensis/050411tusd2335m3.jpg)*

![](actiniaria/magnifica/040522kusbd0005m3.jpg)

![](actiniaria/haddoni/050724bbd5311m3a.jpg)  
[Haddon''s carpet anemone](actiniaria/haddoni.htm)

![](actiniaria/doreensis/050411tusd2335m3a.jpg)  
[Snaky anemone](actiniaria/doreensis.htm)

![](actiniaria/magnifica/040522kusbd0005m3b.jpg)  
[Magnificent anemone](actiniaria/magnifica.htm)

---

These are [soft
corals](coralsoft/coralsoft.htm) with a close up look at their polyps.  
![](coralsoft/letomelette/040423sntd0079m3.jpg)
![](coralsoft/letpimply/070704jngg1231m3a.jpg)
![](coralsoft/nepasparagus/080208hntd9470m3.jpg)
![](coralsoft/letomelette/040423sntd0085m3a.jpg)
![](coralsoft/letpimply/070704jngg1232m3a.jpg)
![](coralsoft/nepasparagus/080208hntd9472m3a.jpg)

---

These are some [hard
corals](coralhard/coralhard.htm) with long polyps or tentacles.  

![](coralhard/fungiidae/heliofungia/040801hntd3805m3.jpg)  
The [Sunflower mushroom
coral](coralhard/fungiidae/heliofungia.htm)   
is a solitary polyp and a hard coral.

![](coralhard/euphylliidae/paraancora/030802hntd0198m3.jpg)  
The [Anchor coral](coralhard/euphylliidae/euphylliidae.htm)
is a colony of polyps  
and is a hard coral.

![](coralhard/euphylliidae/ancora/080605hntd4921m3.jpg)  
The [Anchor
coral](coralhard/euphylliidae/euphylliidae.htm) is a colony of polyps and is a hard coral.

![](coralhard/fungiidae/heliofungia/040801hntd3805m3a.jpg)

![](coralhard/euphylliidae/paraancora/030802hntd0198m3b.jpg)

![](coralhard/euphylliidae/ancora/080605hntd4921m3a.jpg)

---

how to tell apart

- [animals
  with a ring of smooth tentacles](cfringtentacles.htm)
- [animals
  with a ring of feathery arms](../glossary/feathery.htm)
- [large
  sea anemones with long tentacles](actiniaria/cfbiglong.htm)
- [large
  sea anemones with short tentacles](actiniaria/stichodactyla.htm)

