****Leaf-like
fishes****How
to tell them apart?*****updated
Sep 2020*   

---

Several different
kinds of fishes are look and behave like leaves.
They are flat, disk-shaped. Some have patterns that resemble dead leaves, others resemble seagrass leaves. Some may also drift with the currents with other dead leaves and other flotsam. Here''s more on
how to tell them apart.

---

![](ephippidae/platax/120408sjid8416.jpg)

![](haemulidae/gibbosus/090806tmd8315m3.jpg)

![](monacanthidae/chinensis/091008tmd2439m3.jpg)

**Juvenile [Batfish](ephippidae/ephippidae.htm)**Family Ephippidae

**Juvenile [Brown sweetlips](haemulidae/gibbosus.htm)**Family Haemulidae

[**Filefish**](monacanthidae/monacanthidae.htm)  
Family Monacanthidae

Drifts with the currents, but can swim away rapidly.
Drifts with the currents, but can swim away rapidly.
''Hangs'' motionless among seaweed and seagrass, but can swim away rapidly.
Very elongated dorsal and
anal fins. Usually with two dark bars, one
through the eye, on an orange body. But patterns can vary.
Disk-shaped, uniformly brownish. Can immediately change to a lighter shade. Tail fin transparent, so at first glance, it appears to have no tail.
Disk-shaped, various colours and patterns, usually blending with its surroundings.

---

****More
comparisons****

---

![](lobotidae/surinamensis/090607tmftd3410m3.jpg)  
[Tripletail](lobotidae/surinamensis.htm) drifts with its head down..   
![](lobotidae/surinamensis/090606tmftd3242m3.jpg)  
[Tripletail](lobotidae/surinamensis.htm) drifts with its head down..
![](drepaneidae/drepane/130811tmftd1284m3.jpg)  
Juvenile [Sicklefish](drepaneidae/drepane.htm).

---

![](monacanthidae/penicilligerus/050511cftd3265m3.jpg)  
[Feathery filefish](monacanthidae/penicilligerus.htm) resembles leaves   
or seaweeds covered in growths.  
*![](monacanthidae/chinensis/110519chgd2112m3.jpg)*A tiny [filefish](monacanthidae/monacanthidae.htm) resembling a seagrass leaf.
![](monacanthidae/chinensis/070702chgg0933m3.jpg)  
[Filefish](monacanthidae/monacanthidae.htm) resembling a seagrass leaf.

---

