INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('articles', '_articles/guides/cfribbon.md', 'cfribbon', 'How to tell apart ribbon-like seagrasses on Singapore shores', 'published', '

seagrasses [text
index](seagrassindex) | [photo index](seagrassfi)
[Seagrasses](seagrass)
**Ribbon-like
seagrasses****How to tell them apart?**  
*updated
Apr 2020*

---

 **Ribbon-like** These different kinds of ribbon-like seagrasses can look very similar.  
Here''s some tips on telling them apart.

---

![](rotundata/060114cjg3880m3.jpg)

![](serrulata/070203smkg7477m3.jpg)

![](thalassia/050513labg6434m3.jpg)

**[Smooth
ribbon seagrass](rotundata)***Cymodocea rotundata*

**[Serrated
ribbon seagrass](serrulata)***Cymodocea serrulata*

**[Sickle
seagrass](thalassia)** *Thalassia hemprichii*

![](rotundata/110929tmftd1579m3.jpg)

*![](serrulata/110830cyrd0552m3a.jpg)*

![](thalassia/110830cyrd0551m3a.jpg)

Leaf
tip rounded or squarish with smooth edge, sometimes with indentation
in the middle.
Leaf
tip rounded with serrated edge.
Leaf
tip rounded.
No
cross hatched veins.
No
cross hatched veins.
Cross
hatched veins.

![](rotundata/060114cjg3880m3a.jpg)

![](serrulata/090503sgwwd0997m3.jpg)

![](thalassia/071026cyrd7071m3a.jpg)

Rhizomes
thick, smooth.
Rhizomes
thick, smooth.
Rhizomes
thick, with leaf scars.

---

![](enhalus/100602tmd5130m3.jpg)

![](halodule/050822cjg2120m3.jpg)

**[Tape
seagrass](enhalus)***Enhalus
acoroides*

**[Needle
seagrass](halodule)** *Halodule*
sp.

![](enhalus/110929tmftd1586m3.jpg)
![](halodule/090706tmftd6593m3.jpg)
 
Leaf
edges are inrolled.
Leaf
with distinct midrib vein. Leaf may be very narrow or broad.

![](enhalus/120219smkd7285m3.jpg)

![](halodule/110830cyrd0555m3.jpg)

 
Leaf
tip rounded smooth.
Leaf
tip with two or three points
 

---

**More
comparisons**

---

![](syringodium/071026cyrd7111m3a.jpg)  
[**Noodle seagrass**](syringodium)   
*Syringodium isoetifolium*

![](ovalis/050428cftg5289m3a.jpg)  
[**Spoon seagrass**](ovalis)   
*Halophila ovalis*

![](beccarii/030913cjd0097m3.jpg)  
[**Beccarri''s seagrass**](beccarii)   
*Halophila beccarri*

Has
cylindrical leaves.

Has
oval leaves.

Has
tiny leaves that   
emerge in a rosette.

---

how to tell apart  [seagrasses from seaweeds](../../glossary/seagrassweed)

**You CAN make a difference for Singapore''s
seagrasses!**[![](../../../Templates/teamsg.jpg)](http://teamseagrass.blogspot.com/)


