Phylum [Cnidaria](cnidaria.htm)
**Animals
with a ring of smooth tentacles  
How
to tell them apart?***updated
Dec 2019*

---

 Several
animals with a central mouth surrounded by a ring of smooth
tentacles are sometimes confused for one another. Here''s more
on how to tell them apart.

---

**![](others/ceriantharia/blackmouth/080422smkd1484m3.jpg)**
![](actiniaria/beadstriped/050426chgg5083m3.jpg)
![](others/zoanthid/zoanthus/040804skdd4111m3b.jpg)

[**Cerianthids**](others/ceriantharia/ceriantharia.htm)  
Order Ceriantharia

[**True
sea anemones**](actiniaria/actiniaria.htm)  
Order Actiniaria

**[Zoanthids](others/zoanthid/zoanthid.htm)**  
Order Zoanthidae

*![](others/ceriantharia/common/120413cjs06290m3.jpg)*
![](actiniaria/beadstriped/050426chgg5083m3a.jpg)
![](others/zoanthid/zoanthus/040804skdd4111m3d.jpg)
Usually
found alone.
Usually
found alone.
Usually
found in groups of many individual polyps. The polyps are joined
to one another.
An outer
ring of longer tentacles and an inner ring of much shorter tentacles.
Various
arrangement of tentacles. Tentacles may be long or short.
Two rows
of tentacles. Tentacles usually very short and of equal length.
Lives inside
a soft tube that it creates.
Does not
live inside a tube.
Does not
live inside a tube.

---

