**Small silvery
fishes   
How
to tell them apart?***updated
Sep 2020*   

---

Several different
kinds of small fishes are silvery.
Here''s more on
how to tell them apart.

---

![](ambassidae/kopsii/050410kusg4216m3.jpg)  
[**Kops'' glass perchelet**](ambassidae/kopsii.htm)   
(*Ambassis kopsii*)  
Family Ambassidae
![](gerreidae/gerreidae/050917smkg2489m3.jpg)  
**[Mojarra](gerreidae/gerreidae.htm)**  
Family Gerreidae   
 
![](ambassidae/kopsii/050410kusg4216m3a.jpg)
![](gerreidae/gerreidae/050917smkg2489m3a.jpg)
 
Dorsal fin deeply notched, with blackish tip.
Dorsal fin single continunous (not notched) with blackish tip.
 

---

**More
comparisons**

---

![](sillaginidae/sillaginidae/081117ecpmd2360m3.jpg)  
**[Whiting](sillaginidae/sillaginidae.htm)**  
Family Sillaginidae  
  
Long, slender body. Long snout.  
![](sillaginidae/sillaginidae/100912kusd1441m3.jpg)  
**[Whiting](sillaginidae/sillaginidae.htm)**  
Family Sillaginidae  
  
Long, slender body. Long snout.  
![](atherinidae/duodecimalis/111213tmftd4612m3.jpg)  
**[Tropical silverside](atherinidae/duodecimalis.htm)**  
*Atherinomorus duodecimalis*  
Family Atherinidae  
  
Long, slender body. Short snout.  
Colours silvery
grey, bluish to   
bright blue.

