Batrachoididae](batrachoididae/batrachoididae.htm) | [Family Serranidae](serranidae/serranidae.htm)

**Fishes
that look like stones****How
to tell them apart?***updated
Sep 2020*

---

 **Stoned** Several different kinds of fishes resemble algae-covered stones and
rubble on the shores. Some are dangerous, others are harmless. Here''s
more on
how to tell them apart.

---

![](batrachoididae/trispinosus/070531sisd1451m3.jpg)

![](scorpaenidae/picta/090923labd1778m3a.jpg)

![](synanceiidae/horrida/060312hntd0311m3.jpg)

**[Toadfish](batrachoididae/batrachoididae.htm)**  
Family Batrachoididae

**[Scorpionfish](scorpaenidae/picta.htm)**   
*Parascorpaena picta*  
Family Scorpaenidae

**[Stonefish](synanceiidae/horrida.htm)**  
*Synanceia horrida*Family Synanceiidae

Not
dangerous.   
But has prickly spines that poke
**Dangerous**  
Toxic stings are painful
**Highly
dangerous**  
Toxic stings can be fatal.
Spiny dorsal fins.
Spiny dorsal fins.
Stout dorsal spines.

![](batrachoididae/trispinosus/070531sisd1451m3a.jpg)

![](scorpaenidae/picta/090923labd1778m3.jpg)

![](synanceiidae/horrida/060811rlhd5897m3b.jpg)

Medium
eyes, not protruding.
Large
bulbous eyes,   
protruding out of the head.
Tiny eyes with a bony bridge between the eyes.
Mouth
horizontal.
Mouth
horizontal.
Downturned
mouth in a frown.

---

![](centrogenyidae/vaigiensis/060612cftg6114m3.jpg)

![](scorpaenidae/longispinis/050623cjg8365m3.jpg)

![](scorpaenidae/diabolus/120818lazd0164m3c.jpg)

[**False
scorpionfish**](centrogenyidae/vaigiensis.htm)  
*Centrogenys vaigiensis*Family Serranidae

[**Longspined
scorpionfish**](scorpaenidae/longispinis.htm)  
*Paracentropogon longispinis*  
Family Scorpaenidae

[**False
stonefish**](scorpaenidae/diabolus.htm)   
*Scorpaenopsis diabolus*  
Family Scorpaenidae

 
 
 
Not
dangerous**.**   
Has prickles that may wound but no toxins.
**Dangerous**  
Toxic stings are painful
**Dangerous**  
Toxic stings are painful

![](centrogenyidae/vaigiensis/060612cftg6114m3a.jpg)

![](scorpaenidae/longispinis/050623cjg8365m3a.jpg)

![](scorpaenidae/diabolus/120818lazd0164m3a.jpg)

Dorsal
fin begins well behind the eyes.
Dorsal
fin begins above the eyes.
Small
eyes, mouth horizontal.
No spines next to the mouth.
A pair of spines next to the mouth.
 
Nose
flaps.
No
nose flaps.
 

---

**More
comparisons**  

---

![](scorpaenidae/picta/110630tmftd4810m3.jpg)  
[Painted
scorpionfish](scorpaenidae/picta.htm) (lower) next to   
[False scorpionfish](centrogenyidae/vaigiensis.htm) (upper).

![](scorpaenidae/picta/110630tmftd4810m3a.jpg)

---

**![](tetraodontidae/patoca/050708labd4747m3.jpg)**The [Pufferfish](tetraodontidae/tetraodontidae.htm) sometimes
lies quietly among
stones. It is not venomous (does not sting),
  
but is poisonous (will kill if you eat it).

![](antennariidae/trisignatus/040803tusd4069m3.jpg)  
The well camouflaged [Frogfish](antennariidae/trisignatus.htm)
  
is harmless.

![](antennariidae/black/050917smkg2506m3.jpg)  
The harmless [Frogfish](antennariidae/black.htm) sometimes resembles a black sponge.

