INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('articles', '_articles/locations/intertidal/southernislands/cyrenereef.md', 'cyrenereef', 'Cyrene (Terumbu Pandan)', 'published', '

[Southern expedition](http://megamarinesurvey.blogspot.sg/search/label/Southern%20Expedition) | mega marine survey [blog](http://megamarinesurvey.blogspot.sg/) | [facebook page](https://www.facebook.com/pages/Mega-Marine-Survey-of-Singapore/136892629681549)

---

## Habitats

Central area sandy with good seagrass meadows, rubbly and rocky on western and eastern tips, rubbly edges sparsely reefy.   
1º 15.476''N 103º 45.402''E   
35ha, 1.1km x 300m
(from [Google Earth](http://www.google.com/earth/index.html) and [Earth Point](http://www.earthpoint.us/Shapes.aspx))  
  
[GIS map of Cyrene](https://images.naturehungry.sg/gismaps/text/cyrene.htm)    courtesy of Dr. D. Kumaran Raju
![](photos/cyrene.jpg)

## Conservation status

Does not appear on the [URA Master Plan 2008](http://www.ura.gov.sg/uramaps/?config=config_preopen.xml&preopen=Master%20Plan) or the [Parks and Waterbodies Plan](http://www.ura.gov.sg/uramaps/?preopen=Special%20and%20Detailed%20Controls%20Plans%20%28SDCP%29).   

## Current conservation activities

- Since 1986, Cyrene Reef is one of the survey sites of [underwater coral reef surveys](http://coralreef.nus.edu.sg/survey/data.htm) by [ReefFriends](http://www.bluewatervolunteers.org/reeffriends/) of [NParks](http://www.nparks.gov.sg/cms/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=120&Itemid=123) and the [Blue Water Volunteers](http://www.bluewatervolunteers.org/). The intertidal area is also regularly surveyed by [wildsingapore](https://images.naturehungry.sg/).
- 2006-now: [TeamSeagrass](http://teamseagrass.blogspot.sg/) with [NParks](http://www.nparks.gov.sg/cms/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=120&Itemid=123) has been monitoring [seagrasses at Cyrene](http://www.seagrasswatch.org/Singapore.html).
- Ad-hoc: Short-term studies of seagrasses, Common sea stars (*Archaster typicus*) and Knobbly sea stars (*Protoreaster nodosus*).
- Ongoing: An effort to bring decision makers in government and corporations[to visit Cyrene](http://cyrenereef.blogspot.sg/).

## About the name

*Terumbu*=A reef or rock at low tide but submerged at high water; *Pandan* probably refers to Sungei Pandan, a river on the mainland that lies north of these reefs. Greek mythology describe Cyrene as an ''extraordinarily beautiful'' woman descended from a river god and a nymph.

---

## Links

- [Cyrene Reef Exposed](http://cyrenereef.blogspot.sg/) a blog documenting efforts to raise awareness about Cyrene.
- [Cyrene Reef](https://images.naturehungry.sg/places/cyrene.htm) on wildsingapore.
- [TeamSeagrass](http://teamseagrass.blogspot.sg/) Volunteer led effort to monitor seagrass meadows in Singapore including [Cyrene](http://teamseagrass.blogspot.sg/search/label/cyrene).
- [Coral Reefs of Singapore](http://coralreef.nus.edu.sg/island/hantu.htm) by Loh Tse-Lynn and the Reef Ecology Study Team, National University of Singapore.
- [Names of (some) Singapore islands](http://habitatnews.nus.edu.sg/articles/singaporeislands/) by Jeffrey Low on habitatnews', '{
