INSERT INTO content_items (collection, path, slug, title, status, body, metadata_json, cover_image, published_at) VALUES ('articles', '_articles/locations/intertidal/southernislands/terumbubemban.md', 'terumbubemban', 'Terumbu Bemban ', 'published', '
[main index](index.html) to Singapore''s Southern shores for the [southern expedition](http://megamarinesurvey.blogspot.sg/search/label/Southern%20Expedition) | mega marine survey [blog](http://megamarinesurvey.blogspot.sg/) | [facebook page](https://www.facebook.com/pages/Mega-Marine-Survey-of-Singapore/136892629681549)

---

**Habitats:**
Central
area sandy, rubbly edges sparsely reefy, small patch of denser corals
(20m) on eastern edge facing Beting Bemban Besar.  
1�
12.624''N 103� 44.452''E  
16ha, 800m x 200m  
(from [Google
Earth](http://www.google.com/earth/index.html) and [Earth
Point](http://www.earthpoint.us/Shapes.aspx))
![](photos/semakau.jpg)
**Conservation
status:** Does not appear on the [URA
Master Plan 2008](http://www.ura.gov.sg/uramaps/?config=config_preopen.xml&preopen=Master%20Plan) or the [Parks
and Waterbodies Plan](http://www.ura.gov.sg/uramaps/?preopen=Special%20and%20Detailed%20Controls%20Plans%20%28SDCP%29).

**Current
conservation activities:** Since
1986, Western Semakau is one of the survey sites of [underwater
coral reef surveys](http://coralreef.nus.edu.sg/survey/data.htm) by [ReefFriends](http://www.bluewatervolunteers.org/reeffriends/)
of [NParks](http://www.nparks.gov.sg/cms/index.php?option=com_content&view=article&id=120&Itemid=123)
and the [Blue Water
Volunteers](http://www.bluewatervolunteers.org/).   
  
The intertidal area of Terumbu Bemban is also regularly surveyed
by [wildsingapore](https://images.naturehungry.sg/).

**About
the name:** *Terumbu*=A reef or rock at
low tide but submerged at high water; *Bemban*=A
type of plant whose stem is used for making baskets, possibly
referring to fish traps.

