Phylum [Cnidaria](cnidaria.htm)
> Class [Anthozoa](anthozoa.htm) > Order [Corallimorphoria](others/corallimorphs/corallimorph.htm)
**Photo
index of cnidarians on Singapore shores** **sea
anemones and anemone-like animals  
polyp diameter 3-5cm short tentacles**

---

*Size given is the
diameter with oral disk expanded*

![](others/corallimorphs/carpet/040410sisbd0053m.jpg)  
  
![](others/corallimorphs/carpet/040705sisd2121m.jpg)  
[Carpet
corallimorph](others/corallimorphs/carpet.htm)  
*Rhodactis indosinensis*

![](others/corallimorphs/beaded/100710sisd8107m.jpg)  
  
![](others/corallimorphs/beaded/060527sjig6070ma.jpg)  
[Beaded
corallimorph](others/corallimorphs/beaded.htm)  
*Discosoma nummiforme*

![](others/corallimorphs/frilled/040817sntd4671m.jpg)  
  
![](others/corallimorphs/frilled/040817sntd4671ma.jpg)  
[Frilled
corallimorph](others/corallimorphs/frilled.htm)  
*Rhodactis inchoata*

![](others/corallimorphs/ridged/050807sjid5569m.jpg)  
  
![](others/corallimorphs/ridged/050807sjid5570m.jpg) [Ridged corallimorphs](others/corallimorphs/ridged.htm)*Platyzoanthus mussoides*

![](others/corallimorphs/stubby/040705sisd2131m.jpg)  
  
![](others/corallimorphs/stubby/040705sisd2131ma.jpg)  
[Stubby corallimorphs](others/corallimorphs/stubby.htm)*Ricordea yuma*

2-4cm.
Oral disk densely covered with short thin tentacles, entire group
looks like a shaggy carpet. Coral rubble. Commonly seen on
our Southern shores.
2-4cm.
Oral disk covered bumps, no tentacles on the edge. Coral rubble. Commonly
seen on our Southern shores.
2-4cm.
Oral disk with fringed edge and covered clusters of very short branched
tentacles. Coral rubble. Commonly seen on our Southern shores.
4-5cm. Oral disk has a ridged surface. Usually a plain unpatterned
brown. Coral rubble. Sometimes seen on our Southern shores.
3-4cm.
Oral disk with short stubby tentacles that also fringe the edge of
the oral disk. Coral rubble. Sometimes seen on our shores.

![](others/corallimorphs/striped/110717tbd7304m.jpg)  
  
![](others/corallimorphs/striped/110717tbd7305m.jpg)  
[Striped  
corallimorphs](others/corallimorphs/striped.htm)*Discosoma* sp.

![](others/corallimorphs/balltip/120410chgd9048m.jpg)  
  
![](others/corallimorphs/balltip/110703cjd5306m.jpg)
  
 [Ball tip corallimorph](others/corallimorphs/balltip.htm)  
*Corynactis* sp

![](others/corallimorphs/whitetip/120607kusd4965m.jpg)  
  
![](others/corallimorphs/whitetip/120721tptd7882m.jpg)  
[White-tip  
corallimorphs](others/corallimorphs/whitetip.htm)*Rhodactis indosinensis*

![](actiniaria/posy/060429skdd1426m.jpg)  
  
![](actiniaria/posy/060429skdd1421mb.jpg)  
[Posy sea anemone](actiniaria/posy.htm)*awaiting identification*

![](actiniaria/tapetum/080720cjd7934m.jpg)  
  
![](actiniaria/tapetum/050428cftg5283m.jpg)  
[Mini
carpet  
anemone](actiniaria/tapetum.htm)  
*Stichodactyal tapetum*

3-4cm.
Oral disk brown with pale stripes, sparse tentacles, smooth edge.
Coral rubble. Sometimes seen on our shores.
1.5-4cm.
Tentacles many, long thin, transparent with darker ball-shaped tip.
Body column smooth and brightly coloured brown, blue, orange or red.
Oral disk usually dark. On rocks. Sometimes seen on our shores.
3-4cm.
Oral disk with short stubby tentacles with white bulbous tips. Coral
rubble. Sometimes seen on our Southern shores.
3-4cm.
Oral disk with short stubby tentacles with bulbous tips. Coral rubble.
Sometimes seen on our Northern shores.
2-6cm.
Tentacles very short, resemble bumps, not so tightly packed together.
In the centre, are neatly arranged into wedge-shaped groups, resembling
the spokes of a wheel. Seagrass meadows. Sometimes seen on
our shores.
  
  
  

