index](cnidariaindex.htm) | [photo index](cnidariafi2.htm)
Phylum [Cnidaria](cnidaria.htm)
> Class [Anthozoa](anthozoa.htm) > Order [Actiniaria](actiniaria/actiniaria.htm)
**Photo
index of cnidarians on Singapore shores**  
**sea anemones and
anemone-like animals  
polyp diameter > 10cm frilly tentacles**

---

*Size given is the
diameter with tentacles expanded*

![](actiniaria/phymanthus/sixpoint/070602sjig9829m.jpg)  
  
![](actiniaria/phymanthus/sixpoint/070602sjig9829mb.jpg)  
[Six-point   
frilly anemone](actiniaria/physixpoint.htm)   
*Phymanthus* sp.

![](actiniaria/phymanthus/band/050808sntg0904m.jpg)  
  
![](actiniaria/phymanthus/band/050808sntg0904mb.jpg)  
[Banded   
frilly anemone](actiniaria/phyband.htm)   
*Phymanthus* sp.

![](actiniaria/phymanthus/plain/060716sisd4623m.jpg)  
  
![](actiniaria/phymanthus/plain/060716sisd4623mc.jpg)  
[Plain   
frilly anemone](actiniaria/phyplain.htm)   
*Phymanthus* sp.

![](actiniaria/phymanthus/smooth/050808sntg0859m.jpg)  
  
![](actiniaria/phymanthus/smooth/050808sntg0859ma.jpg)  
[Smooth   
frilly anemone](actiniaria/physmooth.htm)   
*Phymanthus* sp.

![](actiniaria/phymanthus/purpletip/050808sntg0899m.jpg)  
  
![](actiniaria/phymanthus/purpletip/050808sntg0899mb.jpg)  
[Purple-tip   
frilly anemone](actiniaria/phypurpletip.htm)   
*Phymanthus* sp.

4-8cm.
Six of the tentacles near the centre usually of a different colour.
Oral disk pale. Coral rubble. Commonly seen on our Southern shores.
8-12cm.
Bright yellow or white branches on tentacles give it a banded look.
Oral disk unpatterned with spots. Coral rubble. Commonly seen on our Southern shores.
8-12cm.
Tentacles uniformly coloured sometimes the ''branches'' are outlined
in white. Oral disk with white bars forming a petal-shaped pattern.
Coral rubble. Commonly seen on our Southern shores.
8-12cm.
Tentacles smooth, but some with small branches visible, most pale
with six coloured ones. Oral disk plain. Coral rubble. Commonly seen
on our Southern shores.

8-12cm.
Tentacles and branches brown, with violet tips. Oral disk with fine
white radiating lines. Coral rubble. Commonly seen on our Southern shores.

![](actiniaria/cryptodendrum/060811rlhd5835m.jpg)  
  
![](actiniaria/cryptodendrum/060811rlhd5729mb.jpg)  
[Pizza anemone](actiniaria/cryptodendrum.htm)  
*Cryptodendrum adhaesivum*

![](actiniaria/actinodendron/030714bbd0002m.jpg)  
  
![](actiniaria/actinodendron/030714bbd0002mb.jpg)  
[Fire anemone](actiniaria/actinodendron.htm)   
*Actinodendron arboreum*

 
 
 
25-30cm.
Oral disk with raised edge and tiny, tightly packed tentacles on the
surface, underside often colourful. Hidden in crevices or under dead
corals. Seen on our Southern shores.
15-20cm.
Fat fleshy tentacles covered with branches. **Stings
painfully.** On sand near coral rubble. Seen on our Southern shores.
 
 
 

